{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers","id":878359,"title":"To Draft a Menagerie of Shapechangers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-29T19:38:33-07:00","id":878359,"title":"To Draft a Menagerie of Shapechangers","content":"I'm really not sure how to open this topic, and I have the strangest nagging feeling that I should be apologizing, but here goes...<br /> <br /> This topic ties into my &quot;How do you hack your setting?&quot; topic over in the generic Chronicles of Darkness forum. I was actually sitting down and thinking about my own setting hacks, and I came to a startling realization... although I know that I want to include multiple kinds of &quot;true&quot; shapeshifter in my version of the setting, I don't actually have any really solid ideas for what those species <i>are</i>. I know that I don't want to use Changing Breeds if I can help it, since I found it... well, let's just say poorly done and move on... but, beyond that, I don't have any solid concepts even for species fluff.<br /> <br /> So, I was wondering if it would be permissible for me to ask interested souls if they'd be willing to loan me their opinions and ideas in brainstorming shapechanging breeds? I wouldn't dream of keeping the ideas all for myself, people are more than willing to make use of this topic to devise and develop shapechangers for their own homebrewed settings, I just... don't really know where to begin doing this kind of thing on my own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T21:59:03-07:00","id":878452,"title":"","content":"War Against The Pure has some fantastic shapeshifters; their bull shifters has since been mentioned elsewhere, and are ostensibly canon. Very cool stuff!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T22:28:26-07:00","id":878469,"title":"","content":"Noble Lions who bear the burden of being taken into a prestigous lineage. Their &quot;thrones&quot; granted them the power to make them as the beasts on their hourse's emblems.<br /> <br /> <br /> A cult who through the drinking of blood and sacrifices imbues their faithful with the power of dragons.<br /> <br /> <br /> There is a... substance, artifical and made by twisted sciences that mutates animals and men...Rumors say that there are turtles who practice martial arts in the sewer.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's of course drinking blood to become a vampire bat....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T22:50:24-07:00","id":878495,"title":"","content":"Wereraptors (the avian kind) who hunt the skies much like the wolves hunt the paths of the earth. Fierce, proud, gifted with keen sight to peer beneath the layers of the mortal world and uncover the ephemeral secrets lying beneath. They yearn for the freedom of the winds and chafe against the laws with which humans would bind them\u2014even as they swoop about from eyries of concrete and glass in pursuit of their prey.<br /> <br /> I'm also working on incorporating the various Fera breeds (and lots of other oWoD elements) into the Chronicles. It would be pretty cool to see what their reinterpreted forms might look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T23:01:14-07:00","id":878512,"title":"","content":"They aren't <i>entirely</i> shapshifters, but I have notes vis-a-vis the Agaras from Over the Edge.<br /> <br /> For those of you unfamiliar, they're the descendants of sinful Muslims who were turned into giant rats with human intelligence by Allah. If they live virtuous lives, their children become more and more human until (in modern days) many of them can get away with baggy coats and hats to cover the tails and ears.<br /> <br /> Of course, this transformation works both ways; so the Agara prostitute/drug addict that's an NPC in one of the adventures? Her kids are going to be giant rats <i>big time</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T00:30:13-07:00","id":878563,"title":"","content":"Some homebrew shapeshifters can be found on these Forums. I'm particularly fond of these:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/8823-new-shifters-the-water-horses\">Water Horses</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/8969-new-shifters-the-selkies\">Selkies</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T00:30:28-07:00","id":878564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=878452#post878452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">War Against The Pure has some fantastic shapeshifters; their bull shifters has since been mentioned elsewhere, and are ostensibly canon. Very cool stuff!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, definitely agreed. I'm not a fan of all of the WATP's officially statted shifters, but the Gudthabak/Baal-Hadad are definitely on my &quot;want&quot; list. I just don't really know what else I want to add... I have some vague interests in the Adjab (? the hyena-shifters), Mkole (were-reptiles) and Rokea (were-sharks) from Apocalypse, but A: my knowledge of them is limited to the 20th edition revision of Changing Breeds, and B: I don't want to directly import Apocalypse's meta-plot, so I'd like to find some unique lore for them if possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T01:44:10-07:00","id":878609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=878495#post878495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wereraptors (the avian kind) who hunt the skies much like the wolves hunt the paths of the earth. Fierce, proud, gifted with keen sight to peer beneath the layers of the mortal world and uncover the ephemeral secrets lying beneath. They yearn for the freedom of the winds and chafe against the laws with which humans would bind them\u2014even as they swoop about from eyries of concrete and glass in pursuit of their prey.<br /> <br /> I'm also working on incorporating the various Fera breeds (and lots of other oWoD elements) into the Chronicles. It would be pretty cool to see what their reinterpreted forms might look like.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given how well you've done other apocalypse things, I really look forward to seeing your CoD incarnation of the Gurahl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T02:24:32-07:00","id":878630,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you like my stuff so far! The Gurahl are pretty awesome. I'll have to give some serious thought to how I'd bring them into Forsaken terms while maintaining what was cool about them.<br /> <br /> For the Mokol\u00e9 equivalents, I'm thinking that &quot;living memory&quot; actually works pretty well for them. It translates almost straight over, only I figure they carry the memory of Pangaea (since Gaia, if She exists\u2014and as far as my own Chronicles settings go, She does\u2014is more distant this time around). They're Pangaeans, in a sense, or descendants of the saurian Dragon Kings that once ruled a Pangaea so far back in the mists of time that not even Father Wolf existed. The beasts of fur and fang that might one day become wolves and their ferocious wolf god were but mewling rats beneath the feet of titans whose voices were as storms and footsteps were as earthquakes. Or so say these newcomers, of course.<br /> <br /> I think their deal might be something along the lines of restoring Pangaea, the Border Marches, as a <i>start</i>. They say that once, all the world was Pangaea. There was no division between realms of Flesh and Spirit. Such a thing is unnatural. In the world's primordial youth, flesh, blood, and ephemera all inhabited one world, the fiercely beating heart of Gaia herself. Something happened to cause this growing rift, until now Pangaea has collapsed entirely, taking with it every legacy of that most ancient world.<br /> <br /> Until now. Memories, like monsters, do not always lie quietly in the earth. Sometimes they emerge, bones of a bygone age, bringing with them tales of oceans that once stood where now nations make war, monsters that blotted out the sun as they thundered across the land, and spirit magic so powerful it shaped the flow of continents. And sometimes, these bones aren't just bones. The memories aren't fossil remnants encased in stone tombs. They live. They grow.<br /> <br /> They Rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T02:53:13-07:00","id":878638,"title":"","content":"The gecko must remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T03:22:52-07:00","id":878645,"title":"","content":"Two notes of caution to consider when coming up with your own changing breed type entities - the first is that peoples' ideas for other animal shapeshifters often fall into the trap of being frankly twee. The Chronicles of Darkness is not really a setting that suits a slew of animal shapeshifters in the manner of a fantasy monster manual's roster under the 'Were-' heading. There's a reason that the three 'shifters' in core Forsaken are horrifying, rage-beset werewolves and two types of animal-based entity that hollow you out and wear your skin like a coat. &quot;I'm an XYZ-shifter and come complete with the standard set of forms for my animal!' is drab and doesn't really gel properly with the setting.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe second is that there are a load of really interesting shapeshifting entities in real world mythology and folklore. Virtually none of these are related to specific-animal-type shapeshifters; those that do have a specific set animal shape they can take are rarely approached as 'were-whatevers'. For some reason people tend to ignore the incredible and bizarre wealth of ideas provided thus and instead go 'I shall create some were-XYZs and bolt them crudely onto the core assumptions of Forsaken'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T05:01:21-07:00","id":878666,"title":"","content":"Salty <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">jiopjp</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T06:15:47-07:00","id":878690,"title":"","content":"Nah, I'm not upset; I just think there's lots of potential for interesting shapechanger-related content for the Chronicles of Darkness but that there are common pitfalls people run into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T17:50:26-07:00","id":880613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=878495#post878495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wereraptors (the avian kind) who hunt the skies much like the wolves hunt the paths of the earth. Fierce, proud, gifted with keen sight to peer beneath the layers of the mortal world and uncover the ephemeral secrets lying beneath. They yearn for the freedom of the winds and chafe against the laws with which humans would bind them\u2014even as they swoop about from eyries of concrete and glass in pursuit of their prey.<br /> <br /> I'm also working on incorporating the various Fera breeds (and lots of other oWoD elements) into the Chronicles. It would be pretty cool to see what their reinterpreted forms might look like.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm curious about the ideas you have for these wereraptors. I'm in the middle of trying to translate the Surthu Athilal to 2E, and Bird in the Sundered World seems to have a decent emphasis on change, fate, and precognition. I can't quite put my finger on what their purpose would be, or how to sum it up. The Wolf Must Hunt, but what do Bird's children do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T18:08:16-07:00","id":880627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=880613#post880613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious about the ideas you have for these wereraptors. I'm in the middle of trying to translate the Surthu Athilal to 2E, and Bird in the Sundered World seems to have a decent emphasis on change, fate, and precognition. I can't quite put my finger on what their purpose would be, or how to sum it up. The Wolf Must Hunt, but what do Bird's children do?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688070-arindhal-the-wind-lords\">Arindhal: The Wind-Lords</a><br /> <br /> I think they hunt, too, just in the realms foreign to wolves. But you could make it more about ruling and shaping the spirit-kingdoms of the skies and the peripheries between earth and sky. They are the lords of the winds, charged with enforcing the laws of the sky: the wind must ever blow, those who are born to fly must do so, and the envious creatures of the earth must never threaten the delicate balance of the skyward kingdoms. That sort of thing. There's room for interpretation here.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T18:43:26-07:00","id":880653,"title":"","content":"Serious question, everyone. The time I've lurked here in the Werewolf forums, combined with the complaints about Changing Breeds and all the micro templates both official and fan-made are motivating me to homebrew a Simplified Shifter Template. Is anyone interested in that? It would be divided into the following sections:<br /> <br /> 1) The central Merit rated from 1 to 5 dots that works like the Powerstat, its inherent advantages and disadvantages. <br /> <br /> 2) Powers and template-specific Merits that all Shifters can acquire.<br /> <br /> 3) Powers and Merits that are either restricted to your chosen animal, or have an additional effect when possessed by a shifter of a specific type (similarly to Contracts in Changeling 2ED)<br /> <br /> 4) A small list of animal types and the modifiers they might apply to your Attributes and Derived Traits<br /> <br /> 5) A discussion and suggestions on how to give your Shifters their own identity that doesn't clash with the tone of the CoD or rely on the lore of Forsaken. This section would include options for cross-over and a list of Bans/Banes/Miscellanous Special Characteristics lifted from real life mythologies with citation of sources.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I should keep Integrity, but I don't want to use Harmony, as that would bring this template closer to Forsaken. I will have to read through Changing Breeds and Forsaken more closely and show the draft to some users before posting a 1.0 version, so this will take a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T18:55:42-07:00","id":880656,"title":"","content":"Skin Thief from Dark Eras and Psychic Vampire from Hurt Locker would probably be a good place to start. I'd certainly love to help out with that, especially since I'm trying to adapt the Gudthabak and Surthu Athilal for the Sundered World setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 05-02-2016, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T22:17:37-07:00","id":880745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=880653#post880653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Serious question, everyone. The time I've lurked here in the Werewolf forums, combined with the complaints about Changing Breeds and all the micro templates both official and fan-made are motivating me to homebrew a Simplified Shifter Template. Is anyone interested in that? It would be divided into the following sections:<br /> <br /> 1) The central Merit rated from 1 to 5 dots that works like the Powerstat, its inherent advantages and disadvantages.<br /> <br /> 2) Powers and template-specific Merits that all Shifters can acquire.<br /> <br /> 3) Powers and Merits that are either restricted to your chosen animal, or have an additional effect when possessed by a shifter of a specific type (similarly to Contracts in Changeling 2ED)<br /> <br /> 4) A small list of animal types and the modifiers they might apply to your Attributes and Derived Traits<br /> <br /> 5) A discussion and suggestions on how to give your Shifters their own identity that doesn't clash with the tone of the CoD or rely on the lore of Forsaken. This section would include options for cross-over and a list of Bans/Banes/Miscellanous Special Characteristics lifted from real life mythologies with citation of sources.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I should keep Integrity, but I don't want to use Harmony, as that would bring this template closer to Forsaken. I will have to read through Changing Breeds and Forsaken more closely and show the draft to some users before posting a 1.0 version, so this will take a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another possibility is making an... &quot;quick assemble&quot; template that has some basics, such as the power stat being universal, but other parts are &quot;made to order&quot; and can be easily swapped in and out as needed.<br /> <br /> <br /> For instance:<br /> <br /> <br /> We can have different &quot;layouts&quot; for default forms: 5 forms line up like werewolves, 3 forms featuring extremes and one hybrid, 2 forms at opposite ends or the like.<br /> <br /> <br /> Next is Integrity, which can be swapped out for Harmony or even a Satiety like stat, where we provide examples of it. Or even say something like Wisdom.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If the template is to be simple and usable, we ought to design it to be flexible, bendable, open to modifications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T03:26:18-07:00","id":880847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=878495#post878495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wereraptors (the avian kind) who hunt the skies much like the wolves hunt the paths of the earth. Fierce, proud, gifted with keen sight to peer beneath the layers of the mortal world and uncover the ephemeral secrets lying beneath. They yearn for the freedom of the winds and chafe against the laws with which humans would bind them\u2014even as they swoop about from eyries of concrete and glass in pursuit of their prey.<br /> <br /> I'm also working on incorporating the various Fera breeds (and lots of other oWoD elements) into the Chronicles. It would be pretty cool to see what their reinterpreted forms might look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will definitely be on the lookout for those conversions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T04:15:58-07:00","id":880866,"title":"","content":"Can some Mod move this thread to the World of Darkness forum? Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T07:22:46-07:00","id":881759,"title":"","content":"Here is one that I designed several years ago, the <b>Suhum Hafrutharra</b>. I personally think they are a good example of a non predatory ( well they are insectivores.. so not entirely true) shape shifter that fits a role more than &quot;OMG SHAPESHIFTORZ&quot;.<br /> <br /> Haven't fully gotten to converting them to 2nd ed rules, but I'm getting there. In fact I could use help on how to make them fit into second ed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/474954-new-shape-shifter-tie-lin\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...hifter-tie-lin</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 05-04-2016, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T07:54:46-07:00","id":881785,"title":"","content":"also, let us never, EVER, forget the most wonderful, beautiful, and amazing shifters of all time. Easily Sikla Alkis.. the Kamathiratha <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaulta5f7.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaulta5f7.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaulta5f7.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaulta5f7.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T09:14:00-07:00","id":881885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=880866#post880866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can some Mod move this thread to the World of Darkness forum? Thanks in advance.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bSince the best rules we have for creating alternate shifters come from a Forsaken supplement (WatP) this is the most appropriate sub-forum for this thread. One has the option of not participating in the thread if they don't care for it.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T09:57:12-07:00","id":881927,"title":"","content":"Though really, it's odd that this would need to be brought up.. it being a thread related to werewolf content... oh well!<br /> <br /> What could be another interesting direction for a shapeshifter race, which I think is ripe for exploration would be some sort of maniform creature created by one of the Idigam- a shape shifter whose animal forms are more.. let us say mutable. How this would work would be tricky, but I have the barest flicker of a concept already in my head.. a sort of protean ( not to be confused with Protean) chimera..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T12:31:17-07:00","id":882089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=881927#post881927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What could be another interesting direction for a shapeshifter race, which I think is ripe for exploration would be some sort of maniform creature created by one of the Idigam- a shape shifter whose animal forms are more.. let us say mutable. How this would work would be tricky, but I have the barest flicker of a concept already in my head.. a sort of protean ( not to be confused with Protean) chimera..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hm, that'll be tricky for sure ruleswise.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mechanically: How about you settle on very basic, broad &quot;forms&quot; and define the variety of traits that can get activated in a given &quot;form&quot;, a base form if you will.<br /> <br /> And every now and again, the shifter discards and draw news traits. maybe rotate out the oldest form trait for a new one every turn, representing constant change.<br /> <br /> They'd be stuff like....<br /> <br /> &quot;Gorila Arms&quot;, &quot;Mammoth Tusks&quot;, &quot;Tentacles&quot; and they provide bonuses in some manner that stack with themselves in case you rolled the same traits. Overall... I think you need 10 or so different traits at least to cycle through to make it work. You can reasonably make 19 or so and have them sync up to a dice table, although if you use the table as a 10 x 10 grid, you'll need duplicates.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I might be mistaking what protean means...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 05-04-2016, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T22:14:55-07:00","id":882562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=882089#post882089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Hm, that'll be tricky for sure ruleswise.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mechanically: How about you settle on very basic, broad &amp;quot;forms&amp;quot; and define the variety of traits that can get activated in a given &amp;quot;form&amp;quot;, a base form if you will.<br /> <br /> And every now and again, the shifter discards and draw news traits. maybe rotate out the oldest form trait for a new one every turn, representing constant change.<br /> <br /> They'd be stuff like....<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Gorila Arms&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Mammoth Tusks&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Tentacles&amp;quot; and they provide bonuses in some manner that stack with themselves in case you rolled the same traits. Overall... I think you need 10 or so different traits at least to cycle through to make it work. You can reasonably make 19 or so and have them sync up to a dice table, although if you use the table as a 10 x 10 grid, you'll need duplicates.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I might be mistaking what protean means...</div> </div> </div> </div>I had ideas like that, though not quite as just &quot;random animal parts&quot;, but more like your suggestion of them gaining ir losing aspects. Perhsps through feeding on Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T22:25:37-07:00","id":882571,"title":"","content":"Hmm, well you could do something like the new skinchanger merit, and allow them to buy partial change as an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T05:11:42-07:00","id":882785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=878645#post878645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason people tend to ignore the incredible and bizarre wealth of ideas provided thus and instead go 'I shall create some were-XYZs and bolt them crudely onto the core assumptions of Forsaken'.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of were-XYZ's, I would actually suggest going the whole hog, and saying they <i>are</i> Uratha - their spiritual predator side just manifests as the &quot;local badass&quot; predatory animal rather than necessarily wolves (and Father/Mother Wolf was actually Father/Mother Hunter).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T09:41:26-07:00","id":883853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=882571#post882571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hmm, well you could do something like the new skinchanger merit, and allow them to buy partial change as an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I considered that, though I am not really fond of the Skinchanger merit for reasons I cannot fully fathom, though I suspect Changing Breeds and Skinchangers built an aversion to it. It's worth for me to look into though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T11:30:14-07:00","id":883927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=881885#post881885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bSince the best rules we have for creating alternate shifters come from a Forsaken supplement (WatP) this is the most appropriate sub-forum for this thread. One has the option of not participating in the thread if they don't care for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Am I to assume that the purpose of this thread is to create antagonists specifically tailored for mass conflict with Forsaken? If so, carry on then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T18:04:05-07:00","id":884209,"title":"","content":"Has anyone here mentioned Skinchangers or Predators? I think both books had a slew of weird and funky concepts a ST might mine directly or use as sources of inspiration in adaptations or cooking up their own stuff whole cloth. I have certainly ported loads of stuff from either book to Requiem, Vigil or wholy homebrew setting games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T10:37:49-07:00","id":884728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=883927#post883927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Am I to assume that the purpose of this thread is to create antagonists specifically tailored for mass conflict with Forsaken? If so, carry on then.</div> </div> </div> </div>The purpose could be that, but since the shifters from WatP needn't specifically be enemies, not sure what you are trying to get at. The purpose of this thread to my knowledge is in compiling a list of custom shifters and since werewolf covers shapeshifters, it is the appropriate forum for this thread.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I guess a sub purpose could be so that a storyteller could have access to a list of cool antagonists to oppose werewolves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T11:05:36-07:00","id":884751,"title":"","content":"I'm addressing that the shapeshifters in WatP were meant to be antagonists; not player characters. Their existence pitted them against uratha, not unlike hosts, because that was Darksider's argument to make keep it on this forum.<br /> <br /> That's not the case, tho.<br /> <br /> Skinchangers and Changing Breeds were blue-books.<br /> <br /> If the shapeshifters you aim to create don't have any link to Forsaken, I'm at a loss for why would you pair them with them.<br /> <br /> Acrozatarim already addressed that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 05-07-2016, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T11:13:41-07:00","id":884760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=884751#post884751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm addressing that the shapeshifters in WatP were meant to be antagonists; not player characters. Their existence pitted them against uratha, not unlike hosts, because that was Darksider's argument to make keep it on this forum.<br /> <br /> That's not the case, tho.<br /> <br /> Skinchangers and Changing Breeds were blue-books.<br /> <br /> If the shapeshifters you aim to create don't have any link to Forsaken, I'm at a loss for why would you pair them with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were bluebooks true, but they did heavily tie with werewolf; so it is still fitting that shape shifting creatures to be discussed here as werewolf is a game with shape shifting protagonists and antagonists. Its easier to have a thread about shapeshifters in a forum about shape shifters is all.<br /> <br /> I mean look at The Unclean, there is nothing that links them to the Uratha save for potential conflict opportunity... at least as far as I recall lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 05-07-2016, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T13:27:56-07:00","id":884853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=884760#post884760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They were bluebooks true, but they did heavily tie with werewolf; so it is still fitting that shape shifting creatures to be discussed here as werewolf is a game with shape shifting protagonists and antagonists. Its easier to have a thread about shapeshifters in a forum about shape shifters is all.<br /> <br /> I mean look at The Unclean, there is nothing that links them to the Uratha save for potential conflict opportunity... at least as far as I recall lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Hunter in Darkness with an infestation of Unclean would think very, very differently.<br /> <br /> It might be easier, but not correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T14:26:08-07:00","id":884902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=884853#post884853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Hunter in Darkness with an infestation of Unclean would think very, very differently.<br /> <br /> It might be easier, but not correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until they learn they are not Hosts, then they will only kill them for violating their territory.<br /> <br /> It's not incorrect either though, so it shouldn't be a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T14:28:47-07:00","id":884908,"title":"","content":"Now another question is,how would the Balam-Colop fit in this Menagerie? they are a little bizarre by Shapeshifter standards, even when you include the strangeness of some Skinchangers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T14:39:47-07:00","id":884919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=884902#post884902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Until they learn they are not Hosts, then they will only kill them for violating their territory.<br /> <br /> It's not incorrect either though, so it shouldn't be a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go read them up if you think they aren't an issue by their mere existence.<br /> <br /> The definition of &quot;not correct&quot; is incorrect, also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T15:01:34-07:00","id":884933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=884919#post884919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Go read them up if you think they aren't an issue by their mere existence.<br /> <br /> The definition of &amp;quot;not correct&amp;quot; is incorrect, also.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I am wrong in saying them upholding their tribal ban is not what they would focus on learning the Unclean were not Hosts? I think killing whatever violates one territory is sacrosanct, regardless what the perpetrators are doing to violate it. Doesn't matter if you are a murderer killing children in the neighborhood or an unfortunate bugman whose method of reproduction is a near uncontrollable spritual contagion.<br /> <br /> Well, I suggest contacting a Moderator and request this thread be moved then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T15:47:06-07:00","id":884966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=884933#post884933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I suggest contacting a Moderator and request this thread be moved then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Done it before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=880866#post880866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can some Mod move this thread to the World of Darkness forum? Thanks in advance.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T15:53:53-07:00","id":884972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/878359-to-draft-a-menagerie-of-shapechangers?p=884966#post884966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Done it before.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I meant another. Don't know if it would do much good, but you you really think this has to be moved, never hurts to try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T09:44:22-07:00","id":886352,"title":"","content":"So, what exactly i